Description: the deep and HDR canvas: every depth and colour state handed to the compositor, described
 An image deeper than 8 bits (16 bit integer, half float, 32 bit integer,
 float, double), or whose profile carries ITU-T H.273 code points (an ICC
 cicp tag, ICC.1:2022 9.2.17) or reaches outside sRGB's gamut, is shown in its
 own depth and colour state, 2D or 3D: its canvas goes to the compositor
 through the GtkGLArea of the edition's GTK 3 (a stereo image's two views, a
 2D image's one picture on a surface of its own), described with its code
 points.  The state is the profile's own code points; sRGB (1/13) and linear
 sRGB (1/8) for GIMP's own profiles; otherwise linear Rec. 2020 (9/8), to
 which the display transform converts after soft-proofing and the display
 filters instead of to the monitor's profile (gimpdisplayshell-deep.c).  The
 depth follows the precision (8 bits, 16 bit integer, half float, float).  The
 compositor converts to each screen; GIMP never tone-maps for a screen.
 .
 Each eye's render cache and picture are CAIRO_FORMAT_RGBA128F, premultiplied,
 rendered through GEGL in floats and uploaded as GL_RGBA32F.  What lies around
 the image is drawn in 8 bit sRGB as ever and converted to the canvas's state
 (a PQ canvas puts its white at 203 cd/m2, Report ITU-R BT.2408).  Cairo's
 pixman clamps floats above 1.0, so the image's samples are copied into the
 cache and composited over the surroundings by GIMP itself wherever the view
 is unrotated on whole pixels.
 .
 Where a depth or a description cannot reach the compositor (the area's error
 GDK_GL_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT: a transfer function the compositor does not
 list, a half float picture no buffer carries) the canvas steps down: a float
 picture to 16 bit integer, then a stereo image to 8 bit sRGB (milestone 1's
 canvas) and a 2D image to the canvas GIMP draws itself; the status bar says so
 once the step is shown, and the reason is in the log.  On X11 a 2D deep image
 gets no area.  8 bit sRGB images, stereo or not, are drawn as in milestones 1
 and 2.  Preferences > Color Management, "Show deep images in their own depth
 and colors" (gimprc deep-canvas, on by default): off, a deep image is drawn
 as before, in GIMP's 8 bit canvas converted to the monitor profile.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 137, the stereo GIMP's milestone 3)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
